module

public import Mathlib

public section

/-!
# Sharp Newtonian Lipschitz coefficient outside Cartesian safety cubes

Two self-contained theorem statements.

The field generated by masses m_i >= 0 at positions a_i in R^3 is
g(z) = -G * sum_i m_i (z-a_i) / ||z-a_i||_2^3.
The Euclidean norm in this formula is represented by the explicit
three-square root. All distances and field differences in the claims
are measured using the Cartesian supremum norm on Fin 3 -> Real.

The coefficient C3 is defined mathematically by the unique root
t of 2t^3 - 8t^2 - 4t + 1 = 0 in [9/50,1/5] and the expression
(2+6t-2t^2)/(1+2t^2)^(5/2).

The first theorem proves exact existence, uniqueness and scalar
maximality. The second proves the global finite-source bound on
the nonconvex exterior of ALL source-centered open cubes (with
boundaries permitted), without assuming the connecting segment is
safe, plus minimality of the universal coefficient already for the
unit one-source instance.

These statements import only Mathlib. The deliberate placeholders
are the comparison challenge, not claims of completed proofs here.
-/

/-- The stationary cubic has one root in the rational bracket. At that
root the stated exact scalar coefficient is maximal on [0,1]. -/
theorem PalomarNewtonian.scalarMaximum :
    ∃ t : ℝ,
      (9 / 50 : ℝ) ≤ t ∧
      t ≤ (1 / 5 : ℝ) ∧
      2 * t ^ 3 - 8 * t ^ 2 - 4 * t + 1 = 0 ∧
      (∀ s : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → s ≤ 1 →
        (2 + 6 * s - 2 * s ^ 2) /
          (Real.sqrt (1 + 2 * s ^ 2)) ^ 5 ≤
        (2 + 6 * t - 2 * t ^ 2) /
          (Real.sqrt (1 + 2 * t ^ 2)) ^ 5) ∧
      (∀ u : ℝ,
        (9 / 50 : ℝ) ≤ u →
        u ≤ (1 / 5 : ℝ) →
        2 * u ^ 3 - 8 * u ^ 2 - 4 * u + 1 = 0 →
        u = t) := by
  sorry

/-- Global Newtonian sensitivity for arbitrary finite masses and source
positions, and exact universality of the coefficient. All distances are
measured in the Cartesian maximum norm; the gravitational field uses
the physical Euclidean radius. The second conjunct proves optimality
universally over configurations (already N=1 suffices), not
optimality separately for every fixed N and every fixed mass layout. -/
theorem PalomarNewtonian.globalCubicSensitivityAndOptimality
    (t : ℝ)
    (htlow : (9 / 50 : ℝ) ≤ t)
    (hthigh : t ≤ (1 / 5 : ℝ))
    (htcubic : 2 * t ^ 3 - 8 * t ^ 2 - 4 * t + 1 = 0) :
    (∀ (n : ℕ) (G M d : ℝ)
      (m : Fin n → ℝ) (a : Fin n → Fin 3 → ℝ)
      (P Q : Fin 3 → ℝ),
      0 ≤ G →
      0 ≤ M →
      0 < d →
      (∀ i : Fin n, 0 ≤ m i ∧ m i ≤ M) →
      (∀ i : Fin n, d ≤ ‖P - a i‖ ∧ d ≤ ‖Q - a i‖) →
      let g : (Fin 3 → ℝ) → (Fin 3 → ℝ) :=
        fun z =>
          ∑ i : Fin n,
            (-(G * m i) /
              (Real.sqrt
                ((z 0 - a i 0) ^ 2 +
                 (z 1 - a i 1) ^ 2 +
                 (z 2 - a i 2) ^ 2)) ^ 3) • (z - a i)
      ‖g P - g Q‖ ≤
        ((n : ℝ) * G * M *
          ((2 + 6 * t - 2 * t ^ 2) /
            (Real.sqrt (1 + 2 * t ^ 2)) ^ 5) / d ^ 3) *
          ‖P - Q‖) ∧
    (∀ K : ℝ,
      (∀ P Q : Fin 3 → ℝ,
        (1 : ℝ) ≤ ‖P‖ →
        (1 : ℝ) ≤ ‖Q‖ →
        ‖(-(1 : ℝ) /
            (Real.sqrt (P 0 ^ 2 + P 1 ^ 2 + P 2 ^ 2)) ^ 3) • P -
          (-(1 : ℝ) /
            (Real.sqrt (Q 0 ^ 2 + Q 1 ^ 2 + Q 2 ^ 2)) ^ 3) • Q‖ ≤
          K * ‖P - Q‖) ↔
      (2 + 6 * t - 2 * t ^ 2) /
        (Real.sqrt (1 + 2 * t ^ 2)) ^ 5 ≤ K) := by
  sorry
